+# BLUE CURRENT V46.25.0 — REVERSIBLE DEPRECATION MANIFEST
+
+## Release scope
+
+V46.21–V46.25 acts on the operator consolidation scorecard while keeping every removal decision reversible.
+
+### V46.21 — Verified Navigation Cleanup
+
+The desktop navigation had 29 entries with 5 true excess duplicates.
+
+This release removes only those verified duplicate links:
+- Autonomous duplicate entries
+- Guests duplicate entry
+- Executive duplicate entry
+- AI Brain duplicate entry
+
+Result:
+- 24 desktop navigation entries
+- 24 unique desktop destinations
+- 0 internal desktop-navigation duplicates
+
+Mobile navigation was already internally unique and was not altered.
+
+### V46.22 — Merge-Candidate Primary Routing
+
+The consolidation engine now resolves mapped merge candidates to their primary surface.
+
+Example:
+
+`reservationYieldCenter → reservationOperationsCenter`
+
+Task/use evidence generated from a merge candidate can therefore be attributed to the primary operator surface instead of creating fragmented analytics.
+
+### V46.23 — Task-Completion Instrumentation
+
+Adds `recordTaskCompletion()` to operator consolidation evidence.
+
+A task completion records:
+- primary surface
+- source surface
+- task ID
+- outcome
+- active role
+- timestamp
+- metadata
+
+This extends the prior open-event evidence into actual task-completion evidence.
+
+### V46.24 — Minimum Evidence Thresholds
+
+Adds explicit review thresholds:
+- 3 observed days
+- 3 open events
+- 1 task completion
+- 1 distinct role
+- 100% manager primary-workflow coverage
+- automatic deletion disabled
+
+These thresholds are review criteria, not deletion triggers.
+
+### V46.25 — Human-Approved Deprecation Manifest
+
+Adds a reversible manifest workflow:
+
+1. Build draft manifest from current deprecation candidates.
+2. Review evidence and primary-workflow coverage.
+3. Require explicit human approval.
+4. Optionally enable a reversible hide-preview feature flag.
+5. Disable preview to immediately restore hidden surfaces.
+
+The manifest policy is:
+
+`human-approved-reversible-hide-before-delete`
+
+Automatic deletion remains disabled.
+
+## UI
+
+Adds the Human-Approved Deprecation Preview center with:
+- manifest status
+- eligible item count
+- approved count
+- hidden-preview count
+- feature-flag state
+- approver
+- evidence thresholds
+- draft / approve / enable / disable controls
+
+## Validation
+
+- `node scripts/maintenance/test-operator-deprecation-manifest.js` passed.
+- Merge candidate routing validated.
+- Task completion evidence validated.
+- Evidence thresholds validated.
+- Feature-flag enable was blocked before approval.
+- Human approval succeeded.
+- Reversible hide preview enabled successfully.
+- Preview disable restored the flagged surfaces.
+- Automatic deletion remained false.
+- Desktop navigation audit:
+  - 24 entries
+  - 24 unique destinations
+  - 0 internal duplicate entries
+- `npm run check` passed:
+  - 826 JavaScript files
+  - 708 client scripts
+  - 5,279 unique HTML IDs
+- Server startup passed as V46.25.0.
+- `/api/health` returned HTTP 200 with database connected and authentication enabled.
+- Authoritative runtime database SHA-256 remained unchanged.
+
+## Safety / fine-comb policy
+
+- No module code is permanently deleted.
+- Approved hiding is reversible.
+- No live restaurant execution behavior changed.
+- Runtime database is not included in this patch.
+- Feature-flag hiding requires human approval.
+
+## Next fine-comb milestone
+
+The next wave should strengthen operator evidence quality before any permanent removal:
+- multi-day evidence windows
+- per-role task completion rates
+- workflow success/failure outcomes
+- time-to-resolution measurement
+- manifest expiry and revalidation
+- explicit owner sign-off per surface
+- first reversible retirement candidate set
+
+Permanent code deletion should remain a separate, later step after a retirement candidate survives the preview period without breaking workflow coverage.
